Relevant columns and how they will be used  

• "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."LANGUAGES"  
  – "repo_name": repo identifier, used to join with licenses and commits  
  – "language": programming‑language information (VARIANT) – we will look for values that include ‘Shell’  

• "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."LICENSES"  
  – "repo_name": join key  
  – "license": filter to ‘apache‑2.0’ (case–insensitive)  

• "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_COMMITS"  
  – "repo_name": join key  
  – "message": the full commit message, length test & first–word exclusion  
  – additional columns are not required for the count but can be projected for exploration  

Main conditions we will ultimately need  
1. LANGUAGES."language" ILIKE '%Shell%'                    -- repositories that contain Shell code  
2. LICENSES."license"  ILIKE 'apache-2.0'                  -- Apache‑2.0 licensed repos  
3. LENGTH(SAMPLE_COMMITS."message") BETWEEN 6 AND 9999     -- message length window (>5 & <10 000)  
4. SAMPLE_COMMITS."message" NOT ILIKE 'merge %'            -- does not start with “merge ”  
   SAMPLE_COMMITS."message" NOT ILIKE 'update %'           -- does not start with “update ”  
   SAMPLE_COMMITS."message" NOT ILIKE 'test %'             -- does not start with “test ”  

(The leading blank after each keyword ensures we exclude the word only when it is the first word; adjust if needed.)

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Below are ten illustrative Snowflake SQL queries (LIMIT 20) that explore the data from simple discovery to a final count.  
All identifiers are wrapped in double quotation marks per requirement.

```sql
-- 1. Description: Peek at a few language entries to understand how “Shell” appears in the column.
SELECT 
  "repo_name", 
  "language"
FROM "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."LANGUAGES"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: Show repositories whose language field mentions “Shell”.
SELECT 
  "repo_name", 
  "language"
FROM "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."LANGUAGES"
WHERE "language" ILIKE '%Shell%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description: Examine licenses of repositories that declare Apache‑2.0.
SELECT 
  "repo_name",
  "license"
FROM "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."LICENSES"
WHERE "license" ILIKE 'apache-2.0'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description: Find repos that are BOTH Apache‑2.0 and list Shell among languages.
SELECT DISTINCT
  l."repo_name"
FROM "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."LANGUAGES"  l
JOIN "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."LICENSES"   s
  ON l."repo_name" = s."repo_name"
WHERE l."language" ILIKE '%Shell%'
  AND s."license"  ILIKE 'apache-2.0'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Description: View a sample of commit messages for those intersecting repos.
SELECT 
  c."repo_name",
  c."message"
FROM "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_COMMITS" c
JOIN (
        SELECT DISTINCT l."repo_name"
        FROM "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."LANGUAGES" l
        JOIN "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."LICENSES"  s
          ON l."repo_name" = s."repo_name"
        WHERE l."language" ILIKE '%Shell%'
          AND s."license"  ILIKE 'apache-2.0'
     ) x
  ON c."repo_name" = x."repo_name"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description: Filter commit messages that are longer than 5 but shorter than 10 000 characters.
SELECT 
  c."repo_name",
  LENGTH(c."message")        AS "msg_len",
  c."message"
FROM "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_COMMITS" c
WHERE LENGTH(c."message") BETWEEN 6 AND 9999
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Description: Exclude commit messages that start with “merge”, “update”, or “test” (case‑insensitive).
SELECT 
  c."repo_name",
  c."message"
FROM "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_COMMITS" c
WHERE LENGTH(c."message") BETWEEN 6 AND 9999
  AND c."message" NOT ILIKE 'merge %'
  AND c."message" NOT ILIKE 'update %'
  AND c."message" NOT ILIKE 'test %'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Description: Combine repository, license, language, and message filters together (sample output).
SELECT 
  c."repo_name",
  c."message"
FROM "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_COMMITS" c
JOIN "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."LANGUAGES"  l
  ON c."repo_name" = l."repo_name"
JOIN "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."LICENSES"   s
  ON c."repo_name" = s."repo_name"
WHERE l."language" ILIKE '%Shell%'
  AND s."license"  ILIKE 'apache-2.0'
  AND LENGTH(c."message") BETWEEN 6 AND 9999
  AND c."message" NOT ILIKE 'merge %'
  AND c."message" NOT ILIKE 'update %'
  AND c."message" NOT ILIKE 'test %'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Description: Display DISTINCT messages (deduplicated) that satisfy all criteria (sample of 20).
SELECT DISTINCT
  c."message"
FROM "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_COMMITS" c
JOIN "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."LANGUAGES"  l
  ON c."repo_name" = l."repo_name"
JOIN "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."LICENSES"   s
  ON c."repo_name" = s."repo_name"
WHERE l."language" ILIKE '%Shell%'
  AND s."license"  ILIKE 'apache-2.0'
  AND LENGTH(c."message") BETWEEN 6 AND 9999
  AND c."message" NOT ILIKE 'merge %'
  AND c."message" NOT ILIKE 'update %'
  AND c."message" NOT ILIKE 'test %'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Description: Final aggregation – count of qualifying commit messages.
SELECT 
  COUNT(*) AS "num_commit_messages"
FROM "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."SAMPLE_COMMITS" c
JOIN "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."LANGUAGES"  l
  ON c."repo_name" = l."repo_name"
JOIN "GITHUB_REPOS"."GITHUB_REPOS"."LICENSES"   s
  ON c."repo_name" = s."repo_name"
WHERE l."language" ILIKE '%Shell%'
  AND s."license"  ILIKE 'apache-2.0'
  AND LENGTH(c."message") BETWEEN 6 AND 9999
  AND c."message" NOT ILIKE 'merge %'
  AND c."message" NOT ILIKE 'update %'
  AND c."message" NOT ILIKE 'test %';
```

These ten queries gradually build an understanding of the data and culminate in retrieving the required count of commit messages that meet all stated conditions.
